<title>FRANCE: London airports lead EU 1997 air cargo growth.</title>
<headline>London airports lead EU 1997 air cargo growth.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The three London airports recorded the highest percentage gain in cargo traffic last month and for the period January-February 1997 over 1996 among the EU's top cargo-handling airports, figures issued by the Paris airports authority (ADP) show.</p>
<p>(in tonnes with percentage change over same 1996)</p>
<p>Airport	 Feb    pct change	 Jan-Feb   pct change</p>
<p>		  1997   on Feb 96	  1997	on Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>London*     118,050  up 6.3		228,203  up 6.9</p>
<p>Frankfurt    98,272  up 5.4		202,048  up 2.9</p>
<p>Amsterdam    86,438  up 4.7		173,357  up 2.4</p>
<p>Paris**	88,069  up  3.8	     169,996  up 2.6</p>
<p>*  includes  Heathrow, Gatwick and Stansted</p>
<p>** includes Charles de Gaulle and Orly</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
